Z||000000||pHoOl||08-06-2000||04:59 PM||||Anybody know what the significance of it is?  Let me describe.  It's a bar on the "running board" when you open the door.  I've noticed that my friend's 84 2m4 has it, and also his 85 GT, but my 88GT doesn't.  The piece also says "Fiero" in it's cool little font.  Anybody know why my 88GT might not have this?  <P>PS. Don't flame me if i'm being dumb and should have known this||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-06-2000||05:26 PM||||Theres nothing dumb about that question! I believe, but am not positive, but I believe that the "Fiero" and "body by Fisher" tabs were on the 84s, and poss. the 85's only. <BR>I love those "fiero" plates, I pulled a bunch out of a boneyard and put them into several of my Fieros...they look cool, nice little touch!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||08-06-2000||05:50 PM||||There for sale on ebay all the time.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||3
Z||000003||Old Lar||08-06-2000||10:23 PM||||Be careful on the Ebay prices.  You should be able to get them from a boneyard for $5-10 a set.  The tan ones are slightly more rare.  <P>While I was out at Twin Lakes Fiero, I pulled a bunch of Fiero panel covers and Body by Fisher covers from his wrecks and stuck them on a shelf in Bob's parts area. He took a bunch to the Michigan show but no one was buying.  At the Dells, prior to Michigan they vanished quickly.  The Body by Fisher were in the 84's.  Too expensive for GM to continue the manufacture of plastic.||||reg||1
