Z||000007||mrfixit58||08-07-2000||08:17 AM||||Here's a restoration tip for those who want to freshen-up those tired "FIERO" and "Body by Fisher" tabs... <P>I pulled a set of tan tabs from a junker the other day. They had a lot of overspray, a few light scratches and were pretty dull. I noticed that the letters were not painted but injected into the piece. I took some 400 grit wet/dry paper and wet sanded them until the surface was clean and smooth. I then used 1000 grit to get a finished surface. I then applied three light coats of spray can clear coat from Dupli-color. After drying, I sanded again with 1000 grit and used a glazing compound to shine them up. They look mirror smooth and as good as new!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000008||bHooper||08-07-2000||09:28 AM||||my 86.5 GT just has black ones, without any wording.<P>those look sweet!  do they have any that say GT?<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||b lo 0||08-07-2000||11:27 AM||||My '85 GT just says "Fiero" on the panel (no Fisher emblem)  They look pretty ratty-maybe I'll fix them up.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">     <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own||||reg||1
Z||000010||286SE'S||08-07-2000||01:39 PM||||I see the FIERO plates on 84 and 85 cars but only the 84's seem to have the "FISHER BODY".<BR>Someone actually paid $62.00 a few months ago on Ebay for a set. Outrageous! But they do look better than the blank panels.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000011||Old Lar||08-07-2000||01:45 PM||||mrfixit58 has the right approach.  I used some fine grit paper on mine, and wet sanded them.  I didn't do the clear coat spray.  The looked a lot better. They get some scuffing getting in and out of your car.  It was such a small touch that looked nice.  For the few cents GM saved by not continuing it was a shame.  Big companies just look at the bottom line and every penny they can cut is money in their pocket.<P><BR>They will come out with a flat blade screw drive.  Just pry up carefully.||||reg||1
